    {
      "v": 13,
      "zh": "将所遇的一切事详细说给他的妻细利斯和他的众朋友听。他的智慧人和他的妻细利斯对他说：「你在末底改面前始而败落，他如果是犹大人，你必不能胜他，终必在他面前败落。」",
      "en": "Haman then related to his wife Zeresh and to all his friends everything that had happened to him. These wise men,[NOTE:1] along with his wife Zeresh, said to him, “If indeed this Mordecai before whom you have begun to fall is Jewish,[NOTE:2] you will not prevail against him. No, you will surely fall before him!”",
      "notes": [
        "Part of the Greek tradition and the Syriac Peshitta understand this word as “friends,” probably reading the Hebrew term רֲכָמָיו (rakhamayv, “his friends”) rather than the reading of the MT חֲכָמָיו (hakhamayv, “his wise men”). Cf. NLT “all his friends”; the two readings appear to be conflated by TEV as “those wise friends of his.”",
        "Heb “from the seed of the Jews”; KJV, ASV similar."
